    'ly5.c.k1000a': 'Walking over 1,000 parts (min)',
    'ly5.rpMade': 'Made with Video Time Study (vts-tool.com) on {date}.',
    'ly5.scenReady': '\u201c{name}\u201d created: move or turn the stations, the gains show at the top.',
    'ly5.help1': 'Current and scenarios, at the top: the same scenarios as the line balancing. Draw today\u2019s layout in Current (plan, stations, paths) and lock it with Lock the reference, in the same bar: it becomes the reference. A new scenario starts from it or from another scenario; its gains against the current layout show at the top.',
    'ly5.help2': '1. Plan (optional): a picture (PNG, JPG), a PDF or an AutoCAD drawing (DXF). For a picture or a PDF, set the scale by clicking both ends of a known distance; a PDF stays sharp when you zoom in. For a DXF, choose the units, the layers, and the blocks that become stations at scale. Under the plan, Plan opacity fades it and Hide the plan takes it away for a moment. The last plans stay in this browser.',
    'ly5.help3': '2. Stations: choose a type and click on the plan to place it, or cut a machine out of the plan (picture or DXF) to move it with its real look. Drag a station to move it, its corner to resize it, its round handle to turn it (15\u00b0 steps, free with Shift), or type its angle.',
    'ly5.help4': '3. Paths: choose an operator and follow the cycle step by step. The banner gives the step, where the operator comes from, and asks for the destination: click the station, on the side where they stand. On the plan, the departure is framed in orange, the destination in green. An empty spot adds a waypoint to go round a machine.',
    'ly5.help5': 'Each leg curves slightly to the right of the way walked: a walk there and back shows as two lines, each with its arrow. Numbers are the steps of the list; a dashed leg is walked without a part.',
    'ly5.help6': 'In a scenario, Move the stations: drag and turn them, the figures before \u2192 after follow every move. What changes lists the stations and the steps that change, Detail by operator gives the distance, footsteps (0.70 m), walking time and cycle. Before / After shows the current layout in place of the scenario. Play shows the operators walking.',
    'ly5.help7': 'Exports: a PDF presentation in A3 landscape of the layout shown, to project or print; the reports from Compare / Reports at the top (the layout, the line balancing or both); and the Layout sheet of the Excel workbook, with the plans. The standard sheets take the distances and the plans.',
    'ly5.help8': 'Ctrl+Z undoes, Ctrl+Y redoes. Arrow keys move the selected station by 10 cm (50 cm with Shift), R turns it by 15\u00b0 (Shift+R the other way), Delete removes it.',
    'ly5.help9': 'The plan stays on your computer: it is kept in this browser, never in the study file. On another computer, load the same file again: the stations stay where they are.',
